{%- comment -%}
  Fyxx: Rewards band (product block)
  Part of the wine-template buy column, directly under the buy buttons.
  Shows the money value the bottle earns back in LoyaltyLion points, the only
  figure that comes straight from the earn rule, with the real Fyxx Rewards
  lockup and, for signed-in members, their designed tier badge.

  Earn rule: points = floor((variant price in JD, VAT stripped) x tier rate).
  Prices are tax-inclusive and points are awarded on the subtotal only, so the
  base is price / vat_divisor (a block setting defaulting to 1.16 for Jordan's
  16% VAT, so a rate change is an admin edit, not a code one). Floor, not round,
  because the band is a promise and must never state more than the customer
  receives. Tier rates: Blue 3, Silver 4, Gold 5, Platinum 5. variant.price is
  in fils, so divide by 100 first. 100 points = 1 JD across the fixed-amount
  rewards, so jd = points / 100, to two decimals.

  Three states:
    Signed out (no customer): "Earn from X JD back[ on this NOUN]" (Blue is the
      lowest of four rates, hence "from"), plus a line that links to sign in and
      sign up. No badge.
    Signed in with a known tier: "You earn X JD back[ on this NOUN]" (the
      member's own rate, no "from"), the tier badge on the right, and a second
      line showing points to the next tier, or a link to all benefits when there
      is no higher tier or the progress fields have not synced yet.
    Signed in with a blank tier (freshly registered, tier not synced yet): the
      "Earn from X" wording and no second line and no badge, so this person is
      never shown a Blue figure as definite or asked to sign in while signed in.

  Noun: the thing the points are earned on. It is the block setting "noun" and
  defaults to EMPTY, so unset it reads "You earn X JD back" with no noun, which
  is never wrong on any product type. Only the wine template sets it (to
  "bottle"), the one category where the word is unambiguous. An unmapped or new
  product type falls through to no noun, never to a noun borrowed from another
  category.

  Exclusion: LoyaltyLion zeroes the rate for anything in the collection
  "ll-fyxx-rewards-exclude". On those products this renders nothing at all. The
  check reads product.collections, so that collection must be published to the
  Online Store channel for it to be visible here.

  No JavaScript: the value reflects the first/selected variant at page load and
  does not recalculate when the variant changes. No font-family is declared.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign excluded = false
  for c in product.collections
    if c.handle == 'll-fyxx-rewards-exclude'
      assign excluded = true
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- unless excluded -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign price_jd = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price | divided_by: 100.0
    assign vat_divisor = block.settings.vat_divisor | default: '1.16' | plus: 0
    if vat_divisor <= 0
      assign vat_divisor = 1.16
    endif

    assign noun = block.settings.noun | default: '' | strip
    comment
      The noun is meant to come from the block setting, but Shopify is not
      syncing JSON template settings from GitHub to the live theme, so the wine
      template's noun setting never lands. Fall back to "bottle" on the wine
      template itself (a stable suffix) so wine keeps "on this bottle". The block
      setting still wins if it is ever present. Every other template stays empty.
    endcomment
    if noun == blank and template.suffix == 'custom-product-wine'
      assign noun = 'bottle'
    endif
    assign base_jd = price_jd | divided_by: vat_divisor

    comment
      loyalty_tier is a typed single_line_text_field, so .value is the documented
      form, but accept the bare form too so a metafield-access change can never
      silently drop every signed-in member into the no-tier (signed-out) state.
    endcomment
    assign tier = ''
    if customer
      assign tier = customer.metafields.loyaltylion.loyalty_tier.value
      if tier == blank
        assign tier = customer.metafields.loyaltylion.loyalty_tier
      endif
      assign tier = tier | strip
    endif

    assign rate = 3
    case tier
      when 'Silver'
        assign rate = 4
      when 'Gold'
        assign rate = 5
      when 'Platinum'
        assign rate = 5
    endcase

    assign points = base_jd | times: rate | floor
    assign jd_whole = points | divided_by: 100.0 | floor
    assign jd_hundreds = jd_whole | times: 100
    assign jd_cents = points | minus: jd_hundreds
    assign jd_cents_padded = jd_cents | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2

    assign signed_in = false
    if customer and tier != blank
      assign signed_in = true
    endif

    assign cdn = 'https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0108/6328/0224/files/'
    case tier
      when 'Silver'
        assign badge_url = cdn | append: 'Silver_Member_Badge.svg?v=1791301196'
        assign badge_w = 206
      when 'Gold'
        assign badge_url = cdn | append: 'Gold_Member_Badge.svg?v=1791301196'
        assign badge_w = 206
      when 'Platinum'
        assign badge_url = cdn | append: 'Platinum_Member_Badge.svg?v=1791301196'
        assign badge_w = 263
      else
        assign badge_url = cdn | append: 'Blue_Member_Badge.svg?v=1791301195'
        assign badge_w = 206
    endcase

    comment
      The two progress metafields are typed too (tier_upgrade_tier_name is a
      single_line_text_field, tier_progress_needed_for_upgrade is number_decimal),
      so prefer .value and fall back to the bare form the same way.
    endcomment
    assign up_name = customer.metafields.loyaltylion.tier_upgrade_tier_name.value
    if up_name == blank
      assign up_name = customer.metafields.loyaltylion.tier_upgrade_tier_name
    endif
    assign up_name = up_name | strip

    assign up_need_raw = customer.metafields.loyaltylion.tier_progress_needed_for_upgrade.value
    if up_need_raw == blank
      assign up_need_raw = customer.metafields.loyaltylion.tier_progress_needed_for_upgrade
    endif
    assign up_need = up_need_raw | plus: 0 | round: 0
  -%}

  <div class="fx-rewards" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    <div class="fx-rewards__head">
      <img class="fx-rewards__logo"
           src="{{ cdn }}Fyxx_Rewrds_Logo_Black.svg?v=1791300915"
           alt="Fyxx Rewards" width="347" height="182">
      {%- if signed_in -%}
        <img class="fx-rewards__badge" src="{{ badge_url }}" alt="{{ tier }} member"
             width="{{ badge_w }}" height="53">
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <p class="fx-rewards__points">{% if signed_in %}You earn{% else %}Earn from{% endif %} {{ jd_whole }}.{{ jd_cents_padded }} JD back{% if noun != blank %} on this {{ noun }}{% endif %}</p>

    {%- if signed_in -%}
      <p class="fx-rewards__sub">{% if up_name != blank and up_need > 0 %}{{ up_need }} points from {{ up_name }}{% else %}<a href="/pages/rewards">See all your benefits</a>{% endif %}</p>
    {%- elsif customer == blank -%}
      <p class="fx-rewards__sub"><a href="{{ routes.account_login_url }}?return_url={{ product.url }}">Sign in</a> to see your rate, or <a href="{{ routes.account_register_url }}?return_url={{ product.url }}">sign up free</a></p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <style>
    .fx-rewards {
      box-sizing: border-box;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      justify-content: center;
      min-height: 146px;
      padding: 18px 20px;
      margin: 4px 0;
      border-radius: 4px;
      background: #F8D3D7;
      color: #100F0D;
    }
    .fx-rewards__head {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 16px;
      margin-bottom: 15px;
    }
    .fx-rewards__logo { display: block; width: 108px; height: auto; flex: none; }
    .fx-rewards__badge { display: block; height: 27px; width: auto; flex: none; }
    .fx-rewards__points { margin: 0; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.3; color: #100F0D; }
    .fx-rewards__sub { margin: 4px 0 0; font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.3; color: rgba(16,15,13,0.7); }
    .fx-rewards__sub a { color: inherit; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  </style>
{%- endunless -%}
